<title>PAKISTAN: Two ships carrying 26,044 T sugar reach Pakistan.</title>
<headline>Two ships carrying 26,044 T sugar reach Pakistan.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two ships carrying 26,044 tonnes of imported crystal white sugar have reached Pakistan's Karachi port, a port official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The Cormorant was likely to start unloading its cargo of 14,044 tonnes of sugar on Wednesday. The Huai Yang would unload its 12,000 tonnes in the next day or two, he said.</p>
<p>A dealer said the sugar had been imported by private traders, but could not identify its origin.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
